  "prefLabel": "Plc 1002.45 Application Processing and Licensing Fees for the Professions Regulated by the Real Estate Commission",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1002.45 Application Processing and Licensing Fees for the Professions Regulated by the Real Estate Commission. The application processing and licensing fees found in Table 1002.45, below, shall apply to the professions regulated by the real estate commission under RSA 331-A:\n\nTable 1002.45 Application Processing and Licensing Fees for the Professions Regulated by the Real Estate Commission\n\nCategory | License Duration | Fee\n\nAssociate, managing, or principal broker license application processing and licensing:\n\nInitial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | 2 years | $121\n\nSalesperson license application processing and licensing:\n\nInitial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | 2 years | $99\n\nTemporary license per RSA 331-A:21 application processing and licensing | max. one year | $40\n\nReal estate firm or branch office application processing and licensing:\n\nInitial, renewal, or reinstatement after expiration of license | 2 years | $121\n\nAmendment to change any part of a real estate firm license, including changing the principal broker of a real estate firm, the managing broker of a real estate firm or branch office, or the trade name, or activating an inactive license or deactivating an active license | $20\n\nSource. #13703, eff 8-1-23; ss by #14290, eff 7-1-25, EXPIRES: 7-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1000.html"
}
